 PCB operations currently return only a final value or a short error\nstring. This makes partial routing, native startup failure, a stalled API, and a\ntransport timeout difficult to distinguish.\n\nAdd a `routing-v1` capability with managed `autoRouting` and `clearRouting`\nrequests. Validate PCB focus and routing arguments, serialize managed routing\noperations per window, classify final native routing statistics, and report\nstages plus a warning when a native call has not returned after 30 seconds.\nThe warning does not cancel the call or release its lock.\n\nPreserve error name, stack, code, cause, details, and execution phase. Capture\nrequest-local console messages and expose routing/layer enums to submitted\nscripts. The `Routing Task...` menu displays the latest locally observed task.\nExisting execute/result/error fields remain supported.\n\nValidation: ESLint, TypeScript, packaging, 21 compiled-gateway tests and one\nHTTP/WebSocket integration test, published under `test/integration` in the\ncompanion Skill change and runnable with `npm run test:gateway`.\nNative V3.2.186 smoke test routed both nets of a four-pad PCB and created two\ntracks. Native `clearRouting('all')` did not settle after 120 seconds; this\nupstream failure is documented separately and is not claimed to be fixed here.\n\nRequires the companion Bridge task API change for remote task queries:\nhttps://github.com/easyeda/easyeda-api-skill/issues/16.\nThat repository disables pull requests, so the complete companion patch and\ntest commands are submitted in the issue. The published harness is at\nhttps://github.com/asmoyou/easyeda-api-skill/tree/2c0a8a5d805d88a6c96fef8ee71184668afdfded/test/integration.\nNative APIs expose no percentage-progress or cancellation callback. Ordinary\nscripts remain executable on older clients without the new routing enums.\n\nNative API reproduction: https://github.com/easyeda/pro-api-sdk/issues/38.\nThis PR improves diagnostics; it does not fix or close the native clearing issue.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T04:16:36Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T04:19:59Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f6def4d162966145d86d2e355b3ca89a9540031f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"asmoyou:feat/routing-task-observability","ref":"feat/routing-task-observability","repo":{"id":1357816149,"node_id":"R_kgDOUO6hVQ","name":"eext-run-api-gateway","full_name":"asmoyou/eext-run-api-gateway","owner":{"login":"asmoyou","id":12567356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTY3MzU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12567356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou","html_url":"https://github.com/asmoyou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asmoyou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"嘉立创EDA专业版扩展：Run API Gateway — 为 AI 编程工具（OpenCode、QwenCode、KimiCode 等）提供 WebSocket API 网关桥接服务的工具。EasyEDA Pro Extension: Run API Gateway — a tool that provides WebSocket API gateway bridging services for AI programming tools (OpenCode, QwenCode, KimiCode, etc.).","homepage":"","language":null,"visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":0,"watchers_count":0,"watchers":0,"open_issues_count":0,"